      "rationale": "BCI defines fixed windows as consisting of a frame and stationary sash.",
      "explanation": "50 mph is inadequate for any commercial application. 75 mph is lower than Gold Label; suitable for standard-grade windows. 120 mph exceeds Gold Label and would require specialized storm-resistant construction. AAMA Gold Label windows must resist at least 94 mph wind pressure without failure, the highest structural rating. AAMA Gold Label = ≥94 mph structural resistance. For typhoon zones exceeding 150 mph, specify reinforced frames or storm glazing.",
