      "explanation": "0.50 cfm exceeds Gold Label (≤0.30 cfm) limit but may pass lower performance classes. 0.15 cfm is an exceptional limit not defined in standard AAMA grading. 1.00 cfm is far too high for any AAMA-certified window. AAMA Gold Label windows are limited to 0.30 cfm (cubic feet per minute) at 25 mph wind speed, the highest performance tier. AAMA Gold Label = ≤0.30 cfm air leakage. Always specify Gold Label for tropical and typhoon-prone regions.",
